Description: This study targets gain-of-function p53 mutations in ovarian cancer, hypothesizing that distinct mutants drive immunosuppression differently. Tailoring combination therapies to specific p53 mutations could turn immune-cold tumors into responsive malignancies, with potential across other cancers.
